    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). The wild rice is the reason it runs where it does. If you want to bring it down, that is the line to look at first.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eWild rice is the expensive ingredient, not the turkey.\u003c/strong\u003e Check the bulk bins and the warehouse club before the boxed brands. If it is out of reach that week, a long grain brown rice will carry the soup at a fraction of the price.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy whole white mushrooms and slice them yourself.\u003c/strong\u003e Pre-sliced costs more per ounce and goes slimy days sooner.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBacon is a seasoning here, not a main.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy a pound, use what the recipe calls for, and freeze the rest in flat portions for the next few batches.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eThe flour and butter roux replaces store-bought thickener.\u003c/strong\u003e Pennies of flour do the job that a can of condensed soup charges you a couple dollars for."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice separately per the package until tender and set it aside. Starting it first gives it time while you build the soup.",
                    "Chop the bacon and render it in your big pot with the olive oil until crisp, then lift the bacon out and leave the fat behind.",
                    "Add the butter, then the diced onion, celery and carrots, and cook until soft. Add the sliced mushrooms and cook until they give up their water and start to brown.",
                    "Stir in the garlic, the dried thyme and the Italian seasoning, then sprinkle the flour over everything and stir for two minutes to cook out the raw taste.",
                    "Pour in the chicken broth slowly while stirring so the roux does not lump, then simmer until it thickens.",
                    "Add the cooked rice, the turkey breast and the heavy cream, warm it through without boiling, then finish with the lemon juice, the reserved bacon, salt and black pepper."
                ],
